  usilic - Text Console Buffer
  version 1.5b-1  20 Mar 2000
  Coded by Taketo Matsubara

  1.  Introduction

  Usilic is a file viewer that works on a text-terminal.  It can be used on
  Linux or FreeBSD

  2.  Environment

  Usilic has been compiled and run on the following environments:

     Linux

           Debian GNU/Linux 2.1
           RedHat Linux v6.0

     FreeBSD

           4.0-RELEASE

  3.  Installation

  Edit config.sh accordingly and then type `make install' as a super
  user.

  4.  ¼Õ¼­

  I make my acknowledgement with thanks to following persons who sent me
  bug reports and suggestions while I have developed usilic.

  Tomio Narita <narita@mt.cs.keio.ac.jp> agreed to add lv to usilic's
  program list.  (Multilingual file viewer lv can be get from the WWW
  page `LV Homepage' http://www.mt.cs.keio.ac.jp/person/narita/lv/)

  Emiko Hall <emhall@ilap.com> pointed out the bug that usilic's Japanese
  manual page can't be displayed on the default environment and reported
  other faults about usage.

  Harumichi Takahashi <hal@terry.nagaokaut.ac.jp> reported the problem
  caused by the fault of description about kon on FreeBSD.

  Kazuhiko Kiriyama <kiri@kiri.toba-cmt.ac.jp> pointed out the
  difficulty of key-assignments.  He tested port and gave me advice
  about it.

  Pierstorff <arne.p@t-online.de> suggested to support function about
  refering to a RPM package and a huge archive file, and pointed out
  incorrect code that fails to compilation.

